  "content": {
    "id": "p107-task59-62-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "For each pair of circles, state how many points of intersection they have.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p107-task59-62-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^2+y^2&=1\\\\x^2+y^2&=4\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p107-task59-62-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "1 point.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p107-task59-62-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Internal tangency: the centre distance equals the radius difference, ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1=2-1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The centres are $(1,0)$ and $(0,0)$, with radii $1$ and $2$ respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=|1-0|\\\\d&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor positive radii and distinct centres, $d<|r_1-r_2|$ places one circle strictly inside the other. At $d=|r_1-r_2|$, they touch internally.\n\nHere $d=1=2-1$, so there is 1 point of intersection, $(2,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p107-task59-62-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^2+y^2&=4\\\\x^2+y^2&=9\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p107-task59-62-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "2 points.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p107-task59-62-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The centre distance lies between the radius difference and sum: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "|3-2|<4<3+2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The centres are $(4,0)$ and $(0,0)$, with radii $2$ and $3$ respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=|4-0|\\\\d&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor positive radii and distinct centres, $|r_1-r_2|<d<r_1+r_2$ gives two intersections: neither circle lies inside the other, and their boundaries cross.\n\nHere $|3-2|<4<3+2$, so there are 2 points of intersection.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p107-task59-62-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^2+y^2&=4\\\\x^2+y^2&=1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p107-task59-62-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "1 point.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p107-task59-62-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "External tangency: the centre distance equals the radius sum, ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "3=2+1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The centres are $(3,0)$ and $(0,0)$, with radii $2$ and $1$ respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=|3-0|\\\\d&=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $d=3=2+1$, the centre distance equals the sum of the radii. The circles touch externally, giving 1 point of intersection, $(1,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p107-task59-62-d",
        "type": "part",
